{{Quote|We held the palace. And then there was a bomb. And when I woke up, it was all just gone.|Zeb Orrelios|<ref name="Legends of the Lasat" />}}
A ''' royal palace''' on [[Lasan]] housed the [[planet]]'s [[Royal family of Lasan|royal family]]. It was protected by the [[Lasan High Honor Guard]], warriors sworn to guard the royal family as well as the people of Lassan. When the [[Galactic Empire]] arrived to [[Siege of Lasan|exterminate]] the [[Lasat]]<ref name="Legends of the Lasat" /> in [[7 BBY]],<ref name="Date" /> the Honor Guard, led by [[Captain]] [[Garazeb Orrelios]], fought to defend the royal palace. However, the Empire prevailed and [[Death|killed]] most of the planet's inhabitants. During the fighting, Orrelios was rendered unconscious in an explosion and woke up to see the palace and his people gone.<ref name="Legends of the Lasat" /> In [[3 BBY]],<ref name="Legends Date">{{RebelsDate|214}}</ref> Orrelios spoke about the battle to his fellow [[Spectres|rebel]] [[Ezra Bridger]], describing the fight for the palace and the aftermath of the siege.<ref name="Legends of the Lasat" />

==Behind the scenes==
The royal palace was first mentioned in "[[Legends of the Lasat]],"<ref name="Legends of the Lasat" /> the fourteenth episode of the [[Star Wars Rebels Season Two|second season]] of the animated television series ''[[Star Wars Rebels]]''.<ref name="Legacy of Lasan">{{WebCite|url=http://affiliate.zap2it.com/tv/star-wars-rebels/EP018796240043?aid=dxd|text=Star Wars Rebels: Legends of the Lasat|work=Disney XD Official Schedule|archivedate=20160407125801}}</ref> The episode aired on [[February 3]], [[2016]].<ref name="Legacy of Lasan">{{WebCite|url=http://affiliate.zap2it.com/tv/star-wars-rebels/EP018796240043?aid=dxd|text=Star Wars Rebels: Legends of the Lasat|work=Disney XD Official Schedule|archivedate=20160407125801}}</ref>

